From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:13:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 38/40] hottyterm: Adwaita Mono is the default font

The built-in font, used when font-family names none or none is found, is
Adwaita Mono (GNOME adwaita-fonts 50.0, SIL OFL 1.1) instead of JetBrains
Mono. hotty-blitz draws surfaces in the same font, from the same release,
so a terminal left at its defaults shows its cells and its surfaces in
one font.

All four static faces are embedded, so bold and italic are the font's
own rather than weights of a variable font. The Inspector draws in it
too. JetBrains Mono stays embedded for the tests only, which reference
it, so it no longer reaches the binary.

Upstream files: a lazy dependency in build.zig.zon (and its URL in
build.zig.zon.txt), four anonymous imports in src/build/SharedDeps.zig,
the default faces in src/font/embedded.zig, the fallback faces in
src/font/SharedGridSet.zig, and one name in src/inspector/Inspector.zig.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
